1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,660
Wait, wait, wait, hold on!

2
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,280
Nogomi, try to calm down.

3
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:12,040
No, no, no, get it down! Roco! Go!

4
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:31,120
Go to the end, gosu jin-sama!

5
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:38,300
Go to the end, gosu jin-sama!

6
00:00:40,313 --> 00:00:45,160
e I geum e

7
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:27,417
false

8
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,717
false false

9
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,537
false false false false

10
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:45,880
What?

11
00:01:45,963 --> 00:01:46,793
You're going to buy
another Oinkie Draw ticket?

12
00:01:46,876 --> 00:01:47,734
What a sweet surprise!

13
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,337
Wisdom number one.

14
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:53,820
Instead of just one person crafting a way,

15
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:58,140
with two sets of hands
there'll be much more pay.

16
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,980
And that, good sir, is
the made way I choose.

17
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,420
Oh, paste away, paste away.

18
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,173
Now, wisdom number two.

19
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:09,560
Um, maybe we should stop, Chief. Why?

20
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,837
Because this song's a total downer.

21
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,940
Oh, paste away, paste away.

22
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:15,356
She's still singing.

23
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,017
So, Chief, how many
more do we have to make?

24
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,917
Each one is a half of a...

25
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,980
So, like a million? A million?

26
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:23,237
Don't worry, it's fine.

27
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:26,077
With five of us, it's
only $200,000 per person.

28
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,777
You don't want to give up on
the cafe, do you, Nagomi, huh?

29
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:30,272
We have to do these now.

30
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,637
If we don't pay the half a million in

31
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,737
interest within the month
for our overdue dues,

32
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,177
they said we have to close shop.

33
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,090
Huh?

34
00:02:36,173 --> 00:02:37,003
That's right.

35
00:02:37,086 --> 00:02:37,957
The clock's already ticking.

36
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:42,517
But we're out of ideas, our only chance
is to move our fingers at lightning speed!

37
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,577
Just a million more.

38
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,517
Make these flowers with all you've got!

39
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,640
The towel has already been rolled!

40
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:50,200
Ah, you mean dice, not towel.

41
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,700
Hi, Nogomi.

42
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,517
Are those new flyers you have?

43
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:00,129
They look a little different
from the flyers you had before.

44
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:02,777
Actually, we can't afford to buy ink,

45
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:06,507
so we're printing them as light
as possible to get by for now.

46
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:10,200
Well, that's original.

47
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:11,970
Thanks.

48
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:13,752
Can I ask you something?

49
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,400
Sure, what is it?

50
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:19,409
What sort of things can we do
to bring in money to our cafe?

51
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,120
Uh, let me see.

52
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,697
I think special events
are always effective.

53
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,737
What kind of events?

54
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,650
For example,

55
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:29,277
we have Cosmo Mellow's stay tomorrow,
and next week it's Kafka Big Bang.

56
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,277
Having fun events really
helps to bring customers in.

57
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,880
Wow, that actually sounds like a blast.

58
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,179
A great idea is the birthday party.

59
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,980
A birthday? If I recall,

60
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,077
your cafe is part of
the Creatureland group,

61
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:45,097
so you might be able to ask
another affiliated cafe for help.

62
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,121
Dream big go-go!

63
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,560
A birthday party? Yes!

64
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,877
Does anyone have a
birthday coming up soon?

65
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:51,790
Count me out.

66
00:03:51,873 --> 00:03:53,457
I don't want you to know
when my birthday is.

67
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:56,717
Like, anyone really gets born
around this time of year.

68
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,740
Actually, I turn 36 in two
days. Wow. In two days?

69
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
That's too funny.

70
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,737
You have your 36th
birthday coming up, Bronco?

71
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:06,197
We have no cash!

72
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,456
Use your pig brains instead of money.

73
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,940
Got that, Ronko? Got it. Understood.

74
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,794
I'll help out as well.

75
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,320
Here, have some grub. What?

76
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,960
This crappy slap again?

77
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:19,977
It's all we have.

78
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,648
Just be glad it has flavor.

79
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,317
Listen, Siobhan, back during
the war, they boiled...

80
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,812
Where's the two newbies?

81
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,413
They're planning Ronko's birthday party.

82
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,975
Do you think they'll be ready in time?

83
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,320
If it helps, I came up with
an idea for a flyer. Oh, wow.

84
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:36,719
Can I take a look?

85
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,590
Oh.

86
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,837
I realize the fact that it lacks impact.

87
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,449
No, it has plenty of that.

88
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,268
I also considered some
potential activities.

89
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:51,320
I'm not exactly sure where
to insert a coin toss game.

90
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,190
Cointess?

91
00:04:54,273 --> 00:04:55,487
That's way too early for me.

92
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:59,217
Sure, maybe one day I might be
intrigued, but considering my age...

93
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:02,177
I don't think age matters
when playing coin toss.

94
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,160
Oh my god!

95
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,637
Anyway, we can't do everything
written on that list!

96
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,249
You really don't think so?

97
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:16,328
Okay then, let's take a look
and try to consolidate it a bit.

98
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:18,420
Don't worry, I'll take care of it.

99
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,640
Um, if it might be feasible,

100
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:25,417
could we get Ronko a birthday
cake or something like that?

101
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,840
A cheap one would do.

102
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:30,210
Huh?

103
00:05:30,293 --> 00:05:32,380
We're living off stir-fried bean sprouts.

104
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:34,537
You think we have the
cash for a stupid cake?

105
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:37,717
But what if Ronko's birthday
party ends up being popular?

106
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,760
Being popular?

107
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,440
Ends up being popular?

108
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:47,417
Who the heck is gonna come
celebrate Ronko's birthday?

109
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,820
You can do whatever.

110
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,475
Just don't cause any problems
with any of our regulars.

111
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:53,730
Problems?

112
00:05:53,813 --> 00:05:56,034
I'm the top earner here at Oinky Doink.

113
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:59,634
Looking after my masters is
what keeps this place going.

114
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,197
Isn't that right, Chief?

115
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,339
Why, of course it is, Lady Yumechi.

116
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:08,737
Irrelevant maid birthdays should be done
quietly off in the corner somewhere.

117
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:09,650
Irrelevant?

118
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:10,563
Hold on, Yumechi.

119
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,177
Shut your mouth, Thunderling!

120
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,977
You two can go off and have
your own party if you want to.

121
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:16,531
Just keep making flowers.

122
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,937
I told her off good, huh, Lady Yumechi?

123
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:20,237
But that's not...

124
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:23,060
Okay, hog heads, time to feed!

125
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,360
That's too funny.

126
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:31,100
How could they say that?

127
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,230
Ronko?

128
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,787
Could you not sleep, Nagomi?

129
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:47,090
Sorry.

130
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,533
I couldn't stop thinking about tomorrow.

131
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,742
Have you been working all night?

132
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:55,237
I figured I should at least get
all of the decorations put up.

133
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,400
Oh, wow.

134
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,092
That's quite impressive.

135
00:06:58,420 --> 00:06:59,540
Can I help at all?

136
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:03,500
I really appreciate it, but
I'm just about finished here.

137
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,600
Oh, okay then.

138
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,960
What can I do to help
get some reservations?

139
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:20,337
So you might be able to ask
another affiliated cafe for help.

140
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:21,361
Dream Big Go Go!

141
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,280
Oh, I know!

142
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,060
Hmm, okay, let's go in.

143
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:36,490
Wooly fluff!

144
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,137
Welcome home, mistresses.

145
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,137
How may I serve you?

146
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:40,657
Oh, no need for that.

147
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:45,300
We're actually from a sister-maid cafe
called the Oinky Doink Cafe. Oh, wow!

148
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,280
A comrade of ours! Oh, yes!

149
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,537
We have an event at 6 o 'clock,

150
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:52,237
and we were hoping to hand out
some flyers, if that's okay.

151
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,150
Miss Karuko!

152
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,340
Of course, that's fine. Great!

153
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,917
Thank you so much, miss.

154
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,497
Actually, we're a little
short-staffed right now.

155
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:04,117
If you don't mind, it would be nice if
you could help us out for a little while.

156
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,077
Of course we can.

157
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,990
Right, Ronco?

158
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,880
If my talents will suffice. Suffice?

159
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,400
That's so mature!

160
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:14,360
It's so lively in here. Yes, it is.

161
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:16,657
It would be great if
even a small percentage

162
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,446
of these masters stopped
by on their way home.

163
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,670
Excuse me!

164
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,317
We're here visiting from Oinky Doink Cafe.

165
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,576
Please take a flyer.

166
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,540
You're having a birthday party?

167
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:28,680
Yes, we are.

168
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,217
Ronko here is celebrating
her birthday today.

169
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,737
We're having a party at 6.

170
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:34,817
It would be great if you could stop by.

171
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:37,520
Sorry. Is something wrong? Wow.

172
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,240
We have the exact same birthday. What?

173
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,620
Today just so happens to be
my birthday party as well.

174
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:47,837
I'm so happy I have the same birthday
as such a lovely fellow maid like you.

175
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:48,750
Holy fluff.

176
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,040
Karuko, happy birthday!

177
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:52,782
Happy birthday!

178
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:56,360
Oh no, I didn't realize that.

179
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,200
I'm, uh, I'm so sorry.

180
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,600
How old are you today, Runco?

181
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,480
I'll be turning 36.

182
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,200
You'll be turning 36?

183
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,980
Rat, ox, tiger?

184
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,840
Oh wow, 15 years older than me!

185
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:10,737
You must have so much experience.

186
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:13,360
Yikes, is she really a 36-year-old maid?

187
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,740
Talk about ripe.

188
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,700
Oh, did that make you angry?

189
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,260
Not even a little.

190
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:25,389
I believe that age has nothing
to do with being a cute maid.

191
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:26,470
Huh?

192
00:09:26,553 --> 00:09:27,383
Oh, I'm sorry.

193
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,980
I didn't hear a word you said.

194
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,986
Let's get out of here, Ronco.

195
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,800
Oh my, leaving already?

196
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:36,817
Didn't you want to hand
out your party flyers?

197
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:40,135
These tiny black and white
flyers with super faint ink.

198
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,700
They have originality.

199
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,140
Very muted originality.

200
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,320
They're fine.

201
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,697
I think it's a wonderful
flyer that shows how

202
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:52,427
passionate Ronco is
about her birthday party.

203
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,480
We should take our leave now.

204
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:02,360
I'm sorry.

205
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,860
This is all my fault. It's not.

206
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:07,340
I really appreciated it. What?

207
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,257
Thank you for doing that.

208
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:10,820
For standing up for me.

209
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,417
Actually, I was really worried?

210
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,977
That you were going to get mad at them!

211
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,884
and go on one of your rampages.

212
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,040
I'm fine.

213
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:21,477
I don't get angry for my own sake.

214
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:22,390
Huh?

215
00:10:22,473 --> 00:10:27,261
If I ever get slightly emotional at all,
it's only because someone insults the cafe.

216
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:28,760
The cafe?

217
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,100
For me personally,

218
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:36,676
I don't know if I can say that I'm
devoted to the oinky-doink just yet.

219
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:39,700
The other cafes are so unfriendly.

220
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:43,808
And honestly, I don't want to
be a part of all this violence.

221
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:46,920
I know that maids have
to fight, but still.

222
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,660
With turf wars intensifying now,

223
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:55,762
I don't think it's realistic to
stick with a zero-violence policy.

224
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,757
Ronko, if you intend on
living your life as a maid,

225
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,311
you will need to be prepared
to take up arms at some point.

226
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:09,465
So you don't like all
the violence, is that it?

227
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,020
It's fine to think that.

228
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,517
If there's one lesson I've learned,

229
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:27,188
it's what you can stand to lose
if you don't stand and fight.

230
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,980
Please excuse me.

231
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:35,260
What the?

232
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,277
What business do you have with us?

233
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,477
Filthy pics I made!

234
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,678
You think you can get cocky with us?

235
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:42,860
Take that!

236
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:59,631
I thought fighting within the
same group violates our code.

237
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,675
I guess you just really pissed me off.

238
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,657
Won't you come with us
for just a little bit?

239
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:06,740
We'll leave left.

240
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,677
It's no use!

241
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:25,701
I can't get out!

242
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,620
Happy birthday, Miss Ronko!

243
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,577
What is the meaning of all this crap?

244
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:35,720
You just had to have the same
birthday as me, silly pig. Huh?

245
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,020
Same birthday?

246
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:42,460
In other words, here in Akiba, we don't
need more than one birthday on the same day.

247
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,440
We don't need?

248
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,577
Everyone was so nice.

249
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:50,737
The other maids who had the same birthday,
well, let's just say they all popped?

250
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:53,137
and disappeared like pretty red bubbles.

251
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:54,050
Wait a second.

252
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:56,613
Are you saying that you killed them all?

253
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:57,820
Holy fluff.

254
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:02,740
It's almost time for it to
begin, isn't it? Huh? Your party?

255
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:04,777
You said it starts at six o 'clock.

256
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:05,690
Wait!

257
00:13:05,773 --> 00:13:06,700
Oh, don't worry.

258
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:09,780
I'll host your big
birthday party right here.

259
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:16,280
It's a special birthday present

260
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:20,937
Wow, your birthday and the day
that you die are going to match.

261
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,460
Hey, my birthday's on April 2nd!

262
